75-59be-a742-b863c4a0e655" :question/math-academy-id "q-102673" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $AB=BA={I}_{2}$\n- $AC=CA={I}_{2}$\n- $C={A}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is false.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is true. As a result, $C={A}^{-1}$ and statement III is true too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-102673/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102673"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71817/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "1cee3227-419b-52dc-85fc-710df84274b8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 